sue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable, 4.5.1.stable, 4.6.stable, 4.7.dev [56f3e2611daadb0b1894b46737ee3000e82e33f9]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (56f3e2611) - Fedora Linux 43 (Forty Three) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 60.39 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a `SoftBody3D` has a low per-point mass, the behavior of Jolt Physics is often erratic, sometimes resulting in the simulation exploding.\n\nHere's what two 50x50 subdivided meshes look like with Jolt Physics, with the following values:\n\n```\nTotal Mass: 1.01 kg\nLinear Stiffness: 0.5\nShrinking Factor: 0.0\nDamping Coefficient: 0.01\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d7bee08-3a77-4d19-917f-e5b9a904c122\n\nHere's what the same setup looks like with Godot Physics:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8cdec7f8-6f80-45bc-9926-55488b04f922\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run the MRP.\n2. Note the right-hand body behaving erratically, often exploding.\n3. Switch to Godot Physics.\n4. Note the bodies being more well-behaved.\n5. Switch back to Jolt Physics.\n6. Reduce the subdivision of the bodies.\n7. Note how it behaves better.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[soft_body_explosion_2026-02-08_20-24-14.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25168843/soft_body_explosion_2026-02-08_20-24-14.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}",